anistic properties with related antibiotics like 红霉素 and 克拉霉素, particularly regarding cytochrome P450 enzyme inhibition. For instance, 大环内酯类药物 as a class can inhibit CYP3A4, thereby increasing serum concentrations of drugs like 卡马西平, which is primarily metabolized via this pathway. Historical case reports document severe carbamazepine toxicity following co-administration with erythromycin, suggesting that even moderate CYP3A4 inhibitors like 阿奇霉素 warrant caution [Data: Entities (10695); Relationships (31619)]. This class-wide risk reinforces the need for prescriber awareness across all macrolides.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Special populations face heightened risks with 阿奇霉素 use\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Certain patient groups, including 肝肾功能下降者 and the elderly, are at increased risk of adverse outcomes from 阿奇霉素. Impaired hepatic or renal clearance may lead to drug accumulation and enhanced toxicity. Clinical guidance explicitly advises against routine use in these populations unless benefits clearly outweigh risks and dose modifications are implemented under medical supervision [Data: Relationships (7507)]. Given the high prevalence of comorbidities in elderly patients—particularly cardiac and hepatic conditions—this represents a significant safety consideration in real-world prescribing.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"地衣芽孢杆菌 and other live biotherapeutics are compromised by 阿奇霉素\",\n            \"explanation\": \"地衣芽孢杆菌, classified as a 活菌制剂, demonstrates significantly reduced therapeutic efficacy when co-administered with 阿奇霉素 due to the antibiotic’s broad-spectrum antimicrobial activity. Data shows frequent inappropriate co-prescription in clinical practice, with 999 documented instances of 地衣芽孢杆菌–左氧氟沙星 pDDIs and 252 involving 阿奇霉素, indicating a systemic issue in antimicrobial stewardship [Data: Entities (4608, 6648); Relationships (34073, 53159)]. To preserve probiotic viability, administration should be